EXPLAIN
100
AcDbText
 10
470.0
 20
39.0
 30
0.0
 40
2.2
  1
1. This sheet runs on 24 V DC, a low voltage. +24 V is the top line and 0 V is the bottom line. F10 to F13 are fuses.
  7
VFFS
 11
470.0
 21
39.0
 31
0.0
100
AcDbText
 73
2
  0
TEXT
  5
283
330
17
100
AcDbEntity
  8
EXPLAIN
100
AcDbText
 10
470.0
 20
34.6
 30
0.0
 40
2.2
  1
2. K0 is the safety relay. It watches the emergency stop S1 and the guard switch S2 through two separate loops (ch. 1 and ch. 2).
  7
VFFS
 11
470.0
 21
34.6
 31
0.0
100
AcDbText
 73
2
  0
TEXT
  5
284
330
17
100
AcDbEntity
  8
EXPLAIN
100
AcDbText
 10
470.0
 20
30.2
 30
0.0
 40
2.2
  1
3. When S1 and S2 are closed and you press reset S3, K0 switches on. It then feeds 24V_SAFE (the PLC outputs) and the KM1 coil.
  7
VFFS
 11
470.0
 21
30.2
 31
0.0
100
AcDbText
 73
2
  0
